    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is anchored today by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries our highest efficiency score of 82.08. Despite facing Rod\u00f3n, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable park factor and a strong dynamic platoon edge, solidifying his role in the lineup. Our most opportunistic start is **Josh Lowe** (70.66), whose efficiency is bolstered by a high-value matchup against Severino; even with the negative adjustment for an elite opposing catcher, **Josh Lowe** remains a premier option due to his ability to contribute across categories. **Nolan Schanuel** also projects well (64.30) against Severino, leveraging his position in the #3 hole to maximize counting stats.\n\nNavigating the deeper end of the roster, **Liam Hicks** (54.43) and **Dominic Smith** (53.57) provide marginal-to-strong value, with **Liam Hicks** gaining significant ground through a positive platoon adjustment despite facing a tough arm in Strider. **Nasim Nunez** (51.41) rounds out the starting group; while his raw speed is highly valued by our front office, his efficiency is slightly constrained today by an unfavorable batting order spot and the defensive capability of the opposing catcher. Among those on the bench, **Jacob Wilson** and **Heliot Ramos** were the closest to cracking the starting nine, but both were narrowly edged out as we prioritized the superior platoon matchups offered to **Dominic Smith** and **Liam Hicks**. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of several core bats, as **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Andy Pages** are inactive due to scheduled off-days, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. With the current lineup, we are effectively balancing our need for daily production against the risk of game cap depletion. No specific weather flags are present for today\u2019s slate, but the efficiency of **Liam Hicks** is the primary risk factor; should Strider command his slider effectively early on, we are prepared to monitor for mid-game substitutions to protect our overall team averages.",
